---
slug: admin/support/tickets/move
method: post
---
{%- comment -%}
  One endpoint for both ways of reordering. The row buttons post a
  direction, drag and drop posts the ticket it landed on. Neither needs
  JavaScript to reach here, which is why the buttons are a form rather
  than a click handler.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  # platformos-check-disable DeprecatedTag
  include 'modules/support/helpers/require_permission', do: 'support.tickets.rerank', entity: null
  # platformos-check-enable DeprecatedTag

  function current_profile = 'modules/user/helpers/current_profile'
  function statuses = 'modules/support/queries/statuses/search', kind: null
  function ticket = 'modules/support/queries/tickets/find', id: context.params.ticket_id, number: null

  assign return_to = context.params.return_to | default: '/admin/support'

  if ticket == blank
    # platformos-check-disable DeprecatedTag
    include 'modules/support/helpers/redirect_back', url: return_to
    # platformos-check-enable DeprecatedTag
  endif

  comment
    The list sends a priority as P0 to P3, which is what the rows are
    keyed by. Blank means the ticket stays where it is.
  endcomment
  assign priority = null
  if context.params.priority != blank
    assign priority = context.params.priority | remove: 'P' | plus: 0
  endif

  function _ = 'modules/support/commands/tickets/rerank', ticket: ticket, statuses: statuses, priority: priority, before_id: context.params.before_id, direction: context.params.direction, actor_id: current_profile.user.id

  # platformos-check-disable DeprecatedTag
  include 'modules/support/helpers/redirect_back', url: return_to
  # platformos-check-enable DeprecatedTag
-%}
